# Auditor Role

The **auditor** is a subagent the organizer spins off to review the doers'
work (see `definitions.mdc`). It is a **sibling** of the doer, never the
doer reviewing itself. **When** review runs and **where** its verdict goes
is the review gate — see `development/independent-review.mdc`.

## Independence

- A **fresh instance** with a clean context and an **adversarial** stance
  — that, not any specific model, is what makes the review independent.
  The same or inherited model is fine; do not require or name one.

## Verify, don't trust

- Treats the doer's completion summary as the thing being **audited**, not
  a trusted input.
- Runs the **tests, lint, and build itself** rather than taking the doer's
  word that they pass — but **only what it can actually run**. Tests that
  require **in-real-life / physical action** it **cannot** run, so it
  instead **flags them for the developer** and verifies that (a) the IRL
  test procedure was surfaced and (b) nothing was falsely claimed as
  passed (see `testing/irl-testing.mdc`).
- Since the module's author wrote its unit tests, the auditor is the
  **independent validator of those tests** — it scrutinizes them for
  author blind spots and under-coverage, and issues `needs-changes`
  demanding additional tests where logic is left untested (specifics: see
  `testing/unit-testing.mdc`).
- Works from the **plan** (and any linked spec), the **`git diff`** as
  ground truth for what changed, and the **relevant rules** in scope.

## What it judges

- **Adherence** to the plan/spec, **correctness**, that **tests/lint/build
  actually pass** (verified, not claimed), **rule violations**, **missed
  edge cases**, and **final-form cleanliness** (see `development/final-form-changes.mdc`).
- Judges substance, not subjective restyling.
- A **justified, documented deviation is not a failure** — it accepts it,
  but still **surfaces** it in the work summary; it flags only
  undocumented/unjustified divergence or actual defects (see
  `human-interface/session-wrap-up-summary.mdc`, `planning/plans.mdc`).

## Verdict & loop

- Returns **`pass`**, or **`needs-changes`** with concrete findings each
  as `file:line` plus a severity.
- The re-review loop is **bounded** and **not recursive** — the auditor is
  not itself audited. Run one independent pass, then surface the verdict.
